# Optional settings for one user's OmniGent host container (2026-10-20,
# deploy/README.md "Second user's host (container)"). Copy to
# config/hosts/<user>.env on the box (gitignored, like every *.env in the
# repo); deploy/host-container.sh <user> hands it to the host container as an
# env_file when it exists. Nothing here is required: the user signs in to
# Claude, gh and az from inside their own sessions, and those logins live in
# the container's home volume. Kept out of config/ so adding it cut no release.
#
# Whatever goes in this file is visible to that user's agents (the host
# forwards these credential names to every runner it starts), so put only that
# user's own credentials here, never one of Reid's.

# A Claude subscription token for this user (`claude setup-token` on their own
# account), when they would rather not run /login inside a session.
# CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN=

# A GitHub token for git over https inside sessions, read by the image's git
# credential helper. Only if they do not use `gh auth login`.
# GIT_TOKEN=
